speechtext:
Mr. Speaker, it is with sadness that I present to the House a petition signed by literally thousands of Canadians.
The petition of the undersigned residents of Canada who now avail themselves of their ancient and undoubted right thus to present a grievance common to your petitioners:
Whereas Croatia instituted a democratic government in a multi-party election conducted in April 1990;
Whereas 94 per cent of the population of Croatia voted for independence;
Whereas Croatians, like all other peoples are entitled to freedom and democracy and their right to self-determination;
Whereas Canada has an international reputation, has the moral authority and as such can initiate this democratic process without compromising world peace;
Wherefore, the undersigned, your petitioners, humbly pray and call upon Parliament to take the initiative in officially recognizing Croatia as an independent and sovereign democratic nation.
This was signed by several thousand petitioners in the last number of months that had hoped to avoid the bloody conflict we are now witnessing.
